        concept="As the number of features grows, data becomes increasingly sparse. Distance metrics become meaningless (all points become equidistant), models need exponentially more data, and overfitting risk increases dramatically.",
        why_matters="In high-dimensional space, distance-based algorithms (KNN, K-Means) fail because 'nearest' loses meaning. Even with enough data, too many features cause overfitting.",
